<title>USA: Automatic Data unit buys Italy's Sicit MT&amp;T.</title>
<headline>Automatic Data unit buys Italy's Sicit MT&amp;T.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Automatic Data Processing Inc said its ADP Dealer Services Group acquired  Sicit MT&amp;T SpA, an Italian dealer management systems provider, for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>With the acquisition, ADP Dealer Services, based in Brussels, has operations in every major European country.</p>
<p>Automatic Data Processing provides computing services to 375,000 clients worldwide, posting annual revenues of more than $3.5 billion.</p>
<p>Its shares were up 1-1/2 at 42 in early afternoon trading on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
